BT
/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 762.8 Tm (3 LED Indicators and Buttons) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 743.9 Tm (3.1 Status LED) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 728.0 Tm (Solid white: the router is working normally and is connected to the internet.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 712.0 Tm (Blinking white: the router is starting up or a firmware update is in progress. Do not) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 696.1 Tm (unplug the router while the LED blinks white.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 680.1 Tm (Solid amber: the router is working but has no internet connection. See section 9.1.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 664.2 Tm (Blinking amber: WPS pairing is active \(up to 2 minutes\).) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 648.2 Tm (Solid red: hardware fault or failed firmware update. See error code E-301 in section) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 632.3 Tm (10.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 616.3 Tm (Off: no power. Check the adapter and the power switch on the back panel.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 597.5 Tm (3.2 Buttons) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 581.5 Tm (Power button: turns the router on or off.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 565.6 Tm (WPS button: press for 2 seconds to start WPS pairing with a device.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 549.6 Tm (RESET button: recessed pin-hole on the back panel. A short press of 1 to 3 seconds) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 533.7 Tm (restarts the router. Holding it for 10 seconds performs a factory reset \(see section) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 517.7 Tm (8\).) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 36 Tm (NetPro X200 User Manual | NP-X200-UM-EN rev C | Page 4 of 14) Tj
ET
