16 0 obj
<< /Length 1403 >>
stream
BT
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 767.1 Tm (4.3 Setup with a web browser) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 751.2 Tm (Connect a computer to a LAN port or to the default Wi-Fi network. Open a browser and go) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 735.2 Tm (to http://192.168.50.1 or http://netpro.home.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 719.3 Tm (The default administrator username is admin and the default password is printed on the) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 703.3 Tm (label on the bottom of the router. You must change the administrator password during) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 687.4 Tm (the first login.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 671.4 Tm (The setup wizard asks for the internet connection type. For PPPoE \(common for DSL and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 655.5 Tm (fiber\), enter the username and password provided by your internet service provider.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 636.6 Tm (4.4 Placement tips) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 620.7 Tm (Place the router in a central, elevated and open location. Keep it at least 1 m away) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 604.7 Tm (from microwaves, cordless phones and baby monitors, which use the 2.4 GHz band.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 588.8 Tm (Point the four external antennas straight up for the best coverage on a single floor.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 572.8 Tm (For multi-floor homes, angle two antennas at 45 degrees.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 36 Tm (NetPro X200 User Manual | NP-X200-UM-EN rev C | Page 6 of 14) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
