18 0 obj
<< /Length 1703 >>
stream
BT
/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 762.8 Tm (5 Wireless Settings) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 743.9 Tm (5.1 Changing the Wi-Fi name and password) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 728.0 Tm (In the web interface go to Wireless > Basic Settings. Enter a new network name \(SSID\)) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 712.0 Tm (and a password of at least 8 characters, then click Save. All devices must reconnect) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 696.1 Tm (with the new password.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 677.2 Tm (5.2 Smart Connect \(band steering\)) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 661.3 Tm (Smart Connect is enabled by default. It uses one network name for both bands and moves) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 645.3 Tm (devices to the best band automatically. To use separate names for 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz, go) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 629.4 Tm (to Wireless > Smart Connect and turn it off.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 610.5 Tm (5.3 Channel and channel width) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 594.6 Tm (Channel selection is Auto by default. If the connection is unstable in a crowded) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 578.6 Tm (building, set the 2.4 GHz channel manually to 1, 6 or 11 and the channel width to 20) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 562.7 Tm (MHz. For 5 GHz, a width of 80 MHz gives the best balance between speed and stability;) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 546.7 Tm (160 MHz is faster but more sensitive to interference.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 527.9 Tm (5.4 Security mode) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 511.9 Tm (The default security mode is WPA2/WPA3 mixed. Older devices that cannot connect may) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 496.0 Tm (need WPA2-Personal \(AES\). Never use open or WEP security.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 36 Tm (NetPro X200 User Manual | NP-X200-UM-EN rev C | Page 7 of 14) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
