24 0 obj
<< /Length 1296 >>
stream
BT
/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 762.8 Tm (8 Factory Reset) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 746.8 Tm (A factory reset erases all settings, including the Wi-Fi name, passwords, parental) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 730.9 Tm (control profiles and port forwarding rules, and restores the factory defaults printed) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 714.9 Tm (on the label.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 696.1 Tm (8.1 Reset with the RESET button) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 680.1 Tm (1. Make sure the router is powered on and the status LED is lit.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 664.2 Tm (2. Use a paper clip to press and hold the RESET button on the back panel for 10) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 648.2 Tm (seconds, until the status LED blinks amber quickly.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 632.3 Tm (3. Release the button. The router restarts, which takes about 2 minutes.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 616.3 Tm (4. Set up the router again as described in section 4.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 597.5 Tm (8.2 Reset from the web interface) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 581.5 Tm (Go to System > Backup and Restore and click Factory Default. Before resetting, you can) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 565.6 Tm (click Save Settings to download a backup file and restore it later.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 36 Tm (NetPro X200 User Manual | NP-X200-UM-EN rev C | Page 10 of 14) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
