stream
BT
/F2 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 762.8 Tm (9 Troubleshooting) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 743.9 Tm (9.1 No internet connection \(status LED solid amber\)) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 728.0 Tm (Restart the modem and then the router. Check that the cable is in the blue WAN port and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 712.0 Tm (not in a LAN port. If your provider uses PPPoE, check the PPPoE username and password) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 696.1 Tm (under Internet > Connection. If the problem continues, contact your internet service) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 680.1 Tm (provider to confirm that the line is active.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 661.3 Tm (9.2 Wi-Fi keeps disconnecting or is slow) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 645.3 Tm (Move the router to a central location away from interference \(see section 4.4\). Update) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 629.4 Tm (to the latest firmware. Set the 2.4 GHz channel manually to 1, 6 or 11 \(section 5.3\).) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 613.4 Tm (For devices that drop the connection, turn off Smart Connect and connect them to the) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 597.5 Tm (2.4 GHz network directly.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 578.6 Tm (9.3 Forgot the administrator password) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 562.7 Tm (The administrator password cannot be recovered. Perform a factory reset \(section 8\) and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 546.7 Tm (set up the router again.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 527.9 Tm (9.4 Cannot open the web interface) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 511.9 Tm (Make sure your computer is connected to the router, then try http://192.168.50.1) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 496.0 Tm (instead of netpro.home. Disable VPN software and clear the browser cache.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 36 Tm (NetPro X200 User Manual | NP-X200-UM-EN rev C | Page 11 of 14) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
